VeridianOS: fix plasma-desktop compiler warnings (deprecated APIs, fallthrough, parentheses)

GCC reported, and this changes:
- -Wdeprecated-declarations QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter()
  (folder/foldermodel.cpp, folder/placesmodel.cpp, landingpage/landingpage.cpp,
  kded/filterproxymodel.cpp x2): ported to beginFilterChange()/endFilterChange().
  In the setters beginFilterChange() now precedes the state change, as Qt
  documents; where the state has already changed (FolderModel::
  invalidateFilterIfComplete, MostUsedModel's source-model switch) the two
  are called back to back. endFilterChange() with its default
  Direction::Both calls the same filter_changed(Rows|Columns) as
  invalidateFilter() (Qt 6.12 qsortfilterproxymodel.cpp). One difference:
  beginFilterChange() builds the proxy's root
  mapping if it does not exist yet (filterAcceptsRow() over all source
  rows); if the proxy had not been queried yet, endFilterChange() then
  reports the difference as rowsRemoved/rowsInserted where
  invalidateFilter() emitted nothing. The resulting rows are the same.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations KLocalizedContext (dateandtime/dtime.cpp,
  emojier/app/emojier.cpp): ported to KLocalization::setupLocalizedContext()
  and KF6::I18nQml added to both targets. setupLocalizedContext() also
  applies TRANSLATION_DOMAIN to the QML context: for the emojier that is the
  application domain it already used; kcm_clock's main.qml has no i18n
  calls. KLocalizedQmlContext also re-evaluates the QML i18n bindings
  when the application's language changes (QEvent::LanguageChange), which
  KLocalizedContext did not. <KLocalizedQmlContext> must be included before <KLocalizedString>
  when TRANSLATION_DOMAIN is defined (otherwise the i18n() macros rewrite
  its i18n*() member declarations), hence its position in both files.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations QMouseEvent 5-argument constructor
  (folder/eventgenerator.cpp): uses the (localPos, scenePos, globalPos)
  constructor with the values the deprecated one filled in (scenePos =
  localPos, globalPos = QCursor::pos(), per Qt 6.12 qevent.cpp).
- -Wdeprecated-declarations QSqlDatabase::exec()
  (recentFiles/ExcludedApplicationsModel.cpp): QSqlQuery(database).exec(),
  which is what QSqlDatabase::exec() wraps. The database's lastError() is no
  longer updated by this query; nothing reads it.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations QVariant::canConvert(int)
  (keyboard/xkboptionsmodel.cpp): canConvert<bool>(). (On top of the
  existing 0002 patch, which touches the same file.)
- -Wdeprecated-declarations libwacom_get_supported_styli() and
  libwacom_stylus_get_for_id() (tablet/kcmtablet.cpp): ported to
  libwacom_get_styli() (libwacom >= 2.14, now required in CMakeLists.txt;
  the sysroot has 2.20), which returns the WacomStylus objects directly. The
  old id lookup assumed the Wacom vendor ID, so non-Wacom styli were missed
  or mismatched; Wacom styli give the same button count as before.
  Also fixes a leak: the WacomDevice from libwacom_new_from_path() was never
  passed to libwacom_destroy(); it is now, and the styli list is free()d as
  libwacom documents.
- -Wimplicit-fallthrough (solid_actions/ActionEditor.cpp): the PropertyCheck
  case intentionally falls into InterfaceCheck (a property check also needs
  the device type); marked [[fallthrough]].
- -Wparentheses (folder/shortcut.cpp): `mods & ~Keypad | key` already
  parsed as `(mods & ~Keypad) | key`, the intent; parentheses added.

